    <preface>
      <p><b>Commonwealth Banks Act 1973</b></p>
      <p><b>No. 18 of 1973</b></p>
      <p><b>AN ACT</b></p>
      <p>To amend the <i>Commonwealth Banks Act </i>1959–1968 to remove the Limitation on the Amount of Housing Loans to Individuals.</p>
      <p>[<i>Assented to 11 April 1973</i>]</p>
      <p>BE IT ENACTED by the Queen, the Senate and the House of Representatives of Australia, as follows:—</p>
      <p><b>Short title and citation.</b></p>
    </preface>
    <body>
      <section eId="sec-1">
        <num>1</num>
        <subsection eId="sec-1__subsec-1">
          <num>1</num>
          <content>
            <p><b>1.</b><b> </b>(1)	This Act may be cited as the <i>Commonwealth Banks Act </i>1973.</p>
          </content>
        </subsection>
        <subsection eId="sec-1__subsec-2">
          <num>2</num>
          <content>
            <p>(2)	The <i>Commonwealth Banks Act </i>1959–1968, as amended by this Act, may be cited as the <i>Commonwealth Banks Act </i>1959–1973.</p>
          </content>
        </subsection>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec-2">
        <num>2</num>
        <heading>Commencement.</heading>
        <content>
          <p><b>2.</b>	This Act shall come into operation on the day on which it receives the Royal Assent.</p>
        </content>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec-3">
        <num>3</num>
        <heading>Amount of loans.</heading>
        <content>
          <p><b>3.</b>	Section 66 of the <i>Commonwealth Banks Act </i>1959–1968 is repealed.</p>
        </content>
      </section>
